    <DataNode elementId="Fatty-acid-phytyl-esters" textLabel="a fatty acid phytyl ester" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="177021" dataSource="ChEBI" />
      <Graphics centerX="500" centerY="540" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="PMN, hawkins, SRI, caspi">Phytyl fatty acid esters (PFAE) are long chain isoprenoid esters consisting of trans-phytol esterified with fatty acids. They are reported to occur in several mosses and algae, in leaves of some higher plants as well as in selected fruits and vegetables. PFAE mainly function as storage forms for free phytol to protect plant cells as phytol shows membrane toxic properties |CITS: [Kraus18]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="Fatty-acid-phytyl-esters" />
